export const body = "<h2>How Confluence saves time on communication</h2>\n\n<p><span class=\"source-divider\" role=\"separator\"></span></p>\n\n<ul><li>Introduction</li><li>How the team used Confluence</li><li>Tips for using Confluence</li><li>Closing words</li></ul>\n\n<h3>Introduction</h3>\n\n<p>Project management is very difficult when multiple disciplines are involved. <em>The project </em>is an end-to-end character project consisting of Concept, Character, Rigging, Animation, and VFX. Last year, the teams switched to Confluence for communication and documentation. This transition <strong>reduced their time spent on the emails by 80%</strong> and provided them with <strong>better tools for file management</strong>.<br></p>\n\n\n<p><sub>Side note</sub><sub>: Confluence didn't decrease their number of emails because it still sent notifications to their mailboxes</sub><sub>.</sub><br></p>\n\n<h3>How the team used Confluence</h3>\n\n<p>At first, the teams used emails for information exchange and files for documentation. But the number of emails became too overwhelming, and the files were hard to manage. Besides, during the work-from-home period, cross-studio communication became a huge challenge due to connection issues.</p>\n\n<p>Fortunately, the team had already been using Confluence, so they decided to send the feedback to artists working remotely via this platform. Then, the producers started to migrate their work to Confluence over time.<br></p>\n\n<p>Below are some common activities that the <em></em>team carried out on Confluence.<strong></strong><br></p>\n\n<p>Track the tasks of their team members<br>Example</p>\n\n<p>Confluence sends a notice email to whoever gets tagged (mentioned).</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/57f6e00fb8da18cd5f91.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/57f6e00fb8da18cd5f91.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"800\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>2</p>\n\n<p>Exchange feedback with comments and images<br>Example</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/74dac2e525bdd3d51047.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/74dac2e525bdd3d51047.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"700\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 2\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>3</p>\n\n<p>Track the changes to documentation via different versions in historyExample</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/4da293796ab2686e0ad1.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/4da293796ab2686e0ad1.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"510\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 3\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>4</p>\n\n<p>Record meeting notes<br>Example</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0b051ce635499fc30625.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0b051ce635499fc30625.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"619\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 4\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>5</p>\n\n<p>Promote newly-released skins<br>Example</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0d8f3820df83692a4c0a.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0d8f3820df83692a4c0a.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"603\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 5\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<h3>Tips for using Confluence</h3>\n\n<p>the two artists designed many pages for <em>the project</em>. By working in a pair, they were able to refine their designs effectively. Below are some techniques they used to improve the user experience of their space.</p>\n\n<ul><li>LANDING PAGE</li></ul>\n\n<p>On the Landing Page, viewers are treated with:</p>\n\n<ul><li>an accordion image slider:<em> </em>showing latest new skins delivered by the <em></em>team</li><li>quick access buttons: helping viewers navigate easily</li></ul>\n\n<p>The page has two colors, gray and yellow, mirroring the <em>game’</em>s logo.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c58a76ef16f3afa28e80.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c58a76ef16f3afa28e80.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"536\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 6\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<ul><li>VISUAL HIERARCHY</li></ul>\n\n<p>Having <strong>a clear visual hierarchy</strong> can help your users navigate your space more easily.<br></p>\n\n<p>You can create text hierarchy with:</p>\n\n<ul><li>size</li><li>color</li><li><strong>bold</strong></li><li><em>italics</em></li><li>underline</li></ul>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/f57152e6dbe99cd0c54e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/f57152e6dbe99cd0c54e.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"451\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 7\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><br></p>\n\n<ul><li>COLORS</li></ul>\n\n<p>Besides, you can use color to denote different items. This way, viewers can make the connection even without reading the texts. But remember to <strong>keep the color codes consistent within each page</strong>.</p>\n\n<p><strong><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/1f72b86b63879ab353d7.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/1f72b86b63879ab353d7.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"618\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 8\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></strong></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/775eba5797554d155761.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/775eba5797554d155761.webp\" width=\"954\" height=\"369\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 9\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<ul><li>1 PICTURE = 1000 WORDS</li></ul>\n\n<p>To artists, <strong>pictures</strong> <strong>are always better</strong>, so add more pictures and reduce texts.<br></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/84df171fa00592c359da.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/84df171fa00592c359da.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"718\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 10\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><br></p>\n\n<ul><li>USING EXPAND</li></ul>\n\n<p><strong>UI Expand</strong><strong> </strong>is among the most useful tools of Confluence; it allows you to adds extra information in various forms, be it words or images.</p>\n\n<p>Here, the team used it to add translation below English texts.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/c6d3702b178854028fec.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/c6d3702b178854028fec.webp\" width=\"1075\" height=\"456\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 11\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>You can also use <strong>UI Expand</strong><strong> </strong>to help viewers filter content by themselves.</p>\n\n<p>For example, in this page, the four QC steps are only visible if you expand their panels. That means people can choose to read specific content at their will.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/2a43e7e9b2d2f205ef14.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/2a43e7e9b2d2f205ef14.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"523\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 12\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><br></p>\n\n<ul><li>DON'T START FROM SCRATCH</li></ul>\n\n<p>When you design a Confluence space for the first time, it can be difficult to even begin. In case you need some inspiration, you can <strong>reference your client's website</strong> (which the <em></em>team did) or <strong>other Confluence spaces</strong>.</p>\n\n<p><sub>Side note</sub><sub>: linking different contents can keep people browsing. This is called \"dynamic content\".</sub></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/library-inline/0ca7e5c82ef057c66085.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/library-inline/0ca7e5c82ef057c66085.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"662\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 13\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<ul><li>BONUS TAB</li></ul>\n\n<p>You can use the <strong>UI Tab</strong> function to organize your content like this panel.</p>\n\n<h3>Closing words</h3>\n\n<p>Thanks to Confluence, the different disciplines across two studios were able to cooperate efficiently on <em>the project</em>. We hope that, with this experience, you can transition to this platform more easily.</p>\n\n\n<p>Thank you for reading and happy producing!</p>";
export const images = ["assets/library-inline/0b051ce635499fc30625.webp", "assets/library-inline/0ca7e5c82ef057c66085.webp", "assets/library-inline/0d8f3820df83692a4c0a.webp", "assets/library-inline/1f72b86b63879ab353d7.webp", "assets/library-inline/2a43e7e9b2d2f205ef14.webp", "assets/library-inline/4da293796ab2686e0ad1.webp", "assets/library-inline/57f6e00fb8da18cd5f91.webp", "assets/library-inline/74dac2e525bdd3d51047.webp", "assets/library-inline/775eba5797554d155761.webp", "assets/library-inline/84df171fa00592c359da.webp", "assets/library-inline/c58a76ef16f3afa28e80.webp", "assets/library-inline/c6d3702b178854028fec.webp", "assets/library-inline/f57152e6dbe99cd0c54e.webp"];
